Excerpts [4] and [2] point to BIBREF7 as the state-of-the-art comparison system. It is a strong, open-sourced, feature-rich logistic regression classifier [2]. Its features include:
- a bag-of-words representation of unigrams and thread length;
- normalised counts of agreements to previous posts;
- counts of non-lexical reference items such as URLs;
- the Coursera forum type in which a thread appeared [2].

The authors chose it because the system and data of BIBREF0, another prior work, were not available for replication [4]. The excerpts do not say whether BIBREF0 performed better.
